{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.antlr.cst\n     2\t  \"The host parser interpreter's generic half (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §4.3,\n     3\t   §5.1, §5.5): assemble sealed source units, parse each with an ANTLR\n     4\t   grammar profile, and export one portable CST packet per unit.\n     5\t\n     6\t   Nothing here knows a language. A grammar profile supplies the host\n     7\t   constructors:\n     8\t\n     9\t     {:grammar-id  string naming grammar revision and tool\n    10\t      :make-lexer  (fn [CharStream] Lexer)\n    11\t      :make-parser (fn [TokenStream] Parser)\n    12\t      :start       (fn [Parser] ParserRuleContext)}\n    13\t\n    14\t   No ANTLR object leaves this namespace: a packet is plain data.\n    15\t\n    16\t   Packet (version 1):\n    17\t\n    18\t     {:yang.cst/version 1\n    19\t      :yang.cst/unit u\n    20\t      :yang.cst/grammar id\n    21\t      :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok | :yang.cst/syntax-error | :yang.cst/source-error\n    22\t      :yang.cst/root 0                       ; ok only\n    23\t      :yang.cst/nodes [record ...]           ; ok only, preorder, id = index\n    24\t      :yang.cst/errors [error ...]           ; non-ok only\n    25\t      :yang.cst/complete true}\n    26\t\n    27\t   Rule record  {:id n :kind :rule :rule \\\"name\\\" :children [ids] :span [s e]}\n    28\t   Token record {:id n :kind :token :type \\\"NAME\\\" :text t :span [s e]}\n    29\t                 plus :synthetic true when the token's text is not the source\n    30\t                 at its span (indentation helpers, EOF); its span is then\n    31\t                 zero-width.\n    32\t   Error record {:kind :syntax-error :message m :line l :column c :span [s e]}\n    33\t\n    34\t   Spans are half-open UTF-8 byte offsets into the sealed source. A unit with\n    35\t   any syntax error yields an error packet and no nodes: never a partial\n    36\t   program.\"\n    37\t  (:import\n    38\t    (java.nio.charset\n    39\t      StandardCharsets)\n    40\t    (org.antlr.v4.runtime\n    41\t      BaseErrorListener\n    42\t      CharStreams\n    43\t      CommonTokenStream\n    44\t      Lexer\n    45\t      Parser\n    46\t      ParserRuleContext\n    47\t      Recognizer\n    48\t      Token)\n    49\t    (org.antlr.v4.runtime.atn\n    50\t      ATN\n    51\t      LexerATNSimulator\n    52\t      ParserATNSimulator\n    53\t      PredictionContextCache)\n    54\t    (org.antlr.v4.runtime.dfa\n    55\t      DFA)\n    56\t    (org.antlr.v4.runtime.tree\n    57\t      ParseTree\n    58\t      TerminalNode)))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(def packet-version 1)\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t;; =============================================================================\n    65\t;; Source coordinates\n    66\t;; =============================================================================\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn- utf8-length\n    69\t  [cp]\n    70\t  (cond (< cp 0x80) 1\n    71\t        (< cp 0x800) 2\n    72\t        (< cp 0x10000) 3\n    73\t        :else 4))\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\t(defn- byte-offsets\n    77\t  \"Byte offset of each code point index of `s`, plus the total at index n.\n    78\t   ANTLR's CodePointCharStream indexes code points.\"\n    79\t  ^longs [^String s]\n    80\t  (let [cps (.toArray (.codePoints s))\n    81\t        n (alength cps)\n    82\t        out (long-array (inc n))]\n    83\t    (loop [i 0\n    84\t           acc 0]\n    85\t      (aset out i acc)\n    86\t      (when (< i n)\n    87\t        (recur (inc i) (+ acc (utf8-length (aget cps i))))))\n    88\t    out))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn- offset-at\n    92\t  [^longs offsets i]\n    93\t  (aget offsets (max 0 (min i (dec (alength offsets))))))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t;; =============================================================================\n    97\t;; Worker: exclusively owned recognizer caches (§4.3)\n    98\t;; =============================================================================\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- fresh-dfa\n   101\t  ^\"[Lorg.antlr.v4.runtime.dfa.DFA;\" [^ATN atn]\n   102\t  (into-array DFA\n   103\t              (map (fn [i] (DFA. (.getDecisionState atn i) i))\n   104\t                   (range (.getNumberOfDecisions atn)))))\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(defn make-worker\n   108\t  \"A host worker for `profile` owning its own DFA and prediction-context\n   109\t   caches, so no parse shares mutable recognizer state with another worker.\n   110\t   The worker is host state owned by one parser stage; it is not data and\n   111\t   never crosses a stream.\"\n   112\t  [profile]\n   113\t  (let [lexer ^Lexer ((:make-lexer profile) (CharStreams/fromString \"\"))\n   114\t        parser ^Parser ((:make-parser profile)\n   115\t                        (CommonTokenStream. lexer))\n   116\t        lexer-atn (.getATN lexer)\n   117\t        parser-atn (.getATN parser)]\n   118\t    {:profile profile,\n   119\t     :lexer-atn lexer-atn,\n   120\t     :lexer-dfa (fresh-dfa lexer-atn),\n   121\t     :lexer-cache (PredictionContextCache.),\n   122\t     :parser-atn parser-atn,\n   123\t     :parser-dfa (fresh-dfa parser-atn),\n   124\t     :parser-cache (PredictionContextCache.)}))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t;; =============================================================================\n   128\t;; Export\n   129\t;; =============================================================================\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- error-listener\n   132\t  \"Collects syntax errors as data into `errors` (a volatile).\"\n   133\t  [errors offsets]\n   134\t  (proxy [BaseErrorListener] []\n   135\t    (syntaxError\n   136\t      [^Recognizer recognizer offending line column msg _e]\n   137\t      (let [span (if (instance? Token offending)\n   138\t                   (let [^Token t offending\n   139\t                    