{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'grammar-checks|targets|grammar|parse' src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc; rg --files build/antlr antlr | head -60; sed -n '500,530p' docs/design/yang.typescript.md; sed -n '1317,1355p' docs/design/yang.php.md\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:8:   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:17:    #?@(:cljd [] :clj [[yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:28:   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:29:                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:30:                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:50:            :yang.frontend/grammar\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:51:            {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:52:             :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:53:             :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1})))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:58:   shell's own reader read, so its parse stage is the identity.  The Python\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:59:   ANTLR frontend is installed where its parser runs (the JVM); elsewhere\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:60:   selecting it answers `unavailable-parser`.  It shows what a submission\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:66:                            :parse identity,\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:69:                           {:parse identity, :lower yang.python/compile})\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:71:                           {:parse identity, :lower yang.php/compile})\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:74:                              {:parse (fn [source]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:75:                                        (python.antlr.parser/parse-source\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:94:   [:yang.frontend/grammar map?]\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:101:(def ^:private grammar-checks\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:102:  \"`[key valid?]` for the grammar package. The lexer and parser names are\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:105:  [[:yang.grammar/package address?]\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:106:   [:yang.grammar/entries #(and (map? %) (seq %))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:107:   [:yang.grammar/export-profile keyword?]])\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:136:          (first-defect (:yang.frontend/grammar m)\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:137:                        grammar-checks\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:138:                        [:yang.frontend/grammar])\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:140:                  (when-not (optional-name? (:yang.frontend/grammar m) k)\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:142:                             {:path [:yang.frontend/grammar k],\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:144:                [:yang.grammar/lexer :yang.grammar/parser])\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:196:   section 3.7 pins (SPI, language, grammar, profiles). Answers\nantlr/python3/manifest.edn\nantlr/python3/Python3Parser.g4\nantlr/python3/Python3Lexer.g4\nbuild/antlr/python3/upstream/Python3Lexer.g4\nbuild/antlr/python3/upstream/Java__Python3ParserBase.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/upstream/Java__Python3LexerBase.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/upstream/Python3Parser.g4\nbuild/antlr/python3/generated-digests.edn\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3ParserBase.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3Parser.tokens\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3LexerBase.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3Lexer.interp\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3Lexer.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3Parser.interp\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3Lexer.tokens\nbuild/antlr/python3/java/yang/python/antlr/gen/Python3Parser.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/grammar/Python3ParserBase.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/grammar/Python3LexerBase.java\nbuild/antlr/python3/grammar/Python3Lexer.g4\nbuild/antlr/python3/grammar/Python3Parser.g4\nprofile.\n\n### 5.3 Predicates and the dialect flag\n\nThe parser uses six base-class methods (`notLineTerminator`, `n`, `p`,\n`notOpenBraceAndNotFunctionAndNotInterface`, `lineTerminatorAhead`,\n`closeBrace`); the lexer base tracks template-string depth and the\nregex-versus-division context. These are internal library execution\n(`yang.antlr.md` 4.3), not callbacks. Upstream provides Java, C# and C++ bases\nonly, so the local parser is JVM-only and Node and Dart go through packets or\na configured service (`yang.antlr.md` 4.1).\n\n`a<b>(c)` cannot be resolved by alternative order. The generated parser takes\na **dialect flag on the worker**, read by a semantic predicate in the pinned\nparser base class: in `:ts` the parse is the reference compiler's (type\narguments when `<...>` is followed by `(`), in `:js` it is relational. This is\nworker configuration, not a callback. The grammar README's two known\nambiguities (`primaryType` decision 11, `singleExpression` decision 236) are\nhandled by pinning the prediction mode and pinning the parse of the ambiguous\nforms by fixture.\n\n### 5.4 The worker and the REPL probe\n\n`yang.antlr.cst/make-worker` with the profile `{:grammar-id :make-lexer\n:make-parser :start (.program p)}`; nothing in `cst.clj` changes. ASI is the\ngrammar's (`eos` predicates), so a REPL completeness probe cannot use \"error\nat EOF\": the probe reparses the snapshot with a trailing `\\n;` sentinel and\nanswers `:incomplete` only when the error set moves to EOF; otherwise the user\nsubmits explicitly (`yang.antlr.md` 5.3).\n\n### 5.5 CST inventory highlights\n## 6. The grammar route and parser worker\n\n- **Package**: `antlr/php/manifest.edn`, from grammars-v4 `php`\n  (`PhpLexer.g4`, `PhpParser.g4`, MIT), vendored verbatim. The one Java\n  helper, `Java/PhpLexerBase.java` (modes HTML, Script, CSS, PHP, Heredoc;\n  `<?=`; heredoc and nowdoc end detection; string-interpolation lexing),\n  carries an explicit MIT notice (Kochurkin and Marianne) and is **vendored**\n  beside the `.g4` files with its notice; it does not share the TypeScript\n  helpers' unresolved-notice situation.\n- `PhpParser.g4` has no superClass and no predicates, so the parser half is\n  action-free on every target and only the lexer base is per-target. Upstream\n  has Java, C#, C++, JavaScript, Python3 and Antlr4ng ports of the base but no\n  Dart, so the local parser is JVM-first; a Node local parser is a later claim\n  via the upstream JavaScript base, never assumed (`yang.antlr.md` 4.2\n  per-target helper versioning applies). The entry rule is `htmlDocument`. The\n  grammar's non-standard `typeParameterListInBrackets` (generics) is refused\n  as `:yang.php/not-php`.\n- **Helper token rewrites**: the helper turns a `?>` close tag into a\n  `SemiColon`-typed token (text `?>` kept, so the exporter sees real text and\n  a non-synthetic span), and constructs or rewrites heredoc end tokens\n  (`identifier + \";\\n\"` or `\"\\n;\"`), which the exporter classifies as\n  synthetic with a zero-width span. There is no helper patch for heredoc ends:\n  the lowering derives heredoc and nowdoc content from the **spans of the body\n  tokens**, never from an end token's text, and handles the close-tag\n  `SemiColon` tokens by type. If a P0 fixture shows the lowering needs a\n  rewritten token's source, the Python-style positioned-token patch is added\n  to the manifest at P0, not later.\n- **Worker**: `yang.antlr.cst/make-worker` unchanged, profile `{:grammar-id\n  :make-lexer :make-parser :start (.htmlDocument p)}`. Mode-dependent tokens\n  (interpolated string parts, heredoc bodies) export as ordinary tokens with\n  real spans.\n- **REPL completeness probe**: PHP has no ASI, but \"error at EOF after a\n  complete `<?php` prefix\" is a reliable `:incomplete` signal only for\n  unbalanced braces and parentheses, so the probe is brace balance plus a\n  reparse, with an explicit-submit fallback.\n\n## 7. CST to UAST and scope analysis\n\n### 7.1 CST inventory highlights\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
