{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"I found three concrete problems: the parity test omits spans and synthetic flags; generation is not ordered before the REPL builds that will import its output; and the add-a-language recipe leaves unconditional imports pointing at omitted targets. The JS code-point stream is real: ANTLR 4.13.2’s `CharStreams.fromString` enables it."}}
