{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc | head -125; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc | head -105; rg -n 'dynamic|warnings|infer' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/*antlr* | head -35; nl -ba deps.edn | sed -n '35,84p'; nl -ba antlr/python3/manifest.edn | tail -18\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n     2\t  \"Slice F3 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.5.6): the Python ANTLR\n     3\t   frontend at the REPL. State persists across submissions, the shell\n     4\t   shows what a submission printed and not its value, a failed round\n     5\t   keeps the session's runtime state as it was, a round parked on a\n     6\t   require commits its frontend session only when it completes, and\n     7\t   `(reset)` and `(vm ...)` start a new process.\n     8\t\n     9\t   The parser is JVM-only, so the session scenarios run on every host\n    10\t   through a binding whose parse stage answers the parser's packets,\n    11\t   precompiled below (each def's docstring is the source the REPL hands\n    12\t   the parser); on the JVM they run through the installed frontend too,\n    13\t   and the packets are checked against the parser so the two cannot\n    14\t   drift. The completeness probe is JVM-only, as the parser is.\"\n    15\t  (:require\n    16\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    17\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    18\t    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    19\t    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    20\t    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    21\t    [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    22\t    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    23\t    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    24\t    [yang.python.antlr.c3-programs :refer [asg call e ex lit op st tc tx vr]]\n    25\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test :refer [packet]]\n    26\t    [yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.repl]\n    27\t    #?@(:cljd [] :clj [[yang.python.antlr.parser :as parser]\n    28\t                       [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as probe]])\n    29\t    [yin.repl :as repl]\n    30\t    [yin.repl.frontends :as frontends]\n    31\t    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    32\t    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t;; =============================================================================\n    36\t;; Precompiled packets\n    37\t;; =============================================================================\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- module\n    40\t  [& stmts]\n    41\t  (packet (-> [:file_input] (into stmts) (conj [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]))))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(def ^:private packets\n    45\t  \"The parser's packet for each line the session scenarios submit; the\n    46\t   REPL hands the parser the line with a newline appended.\"\n    47\t  {\"x = 1\" (module (st (asg (tc (vr \"x\")) (tc (lit \"1\"))))),\n    48\t   \"x = 5\" (module (st (asg (tc (vr \"x\")) (tc (lit \"5\"))))),\n    49\t   \"print(x)\" (module (st (ex (tc (call \"print\" (tc (vr \"x\"))))))),\n    50\t   \"1/0\" (module (st (ex (tx (op (e (lit \"1\")) \"/\" (e (lit \"0\")))))))})\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t;; =============================================================================\n    54\t;; Sessions\n    55\t;; =============================================================================\n    56\t\n    57\t(def ^:private cst-manifest\n    58\t  {:yang.frontend/id :yang.python/cst,\n    59\t   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n    60\t   :yang.frontend/revision \"f3-test\",\n    61\t   :yang.frontend/language :python.cst,\n    62\t   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n    63\t                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n    64\t                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n    65\t   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n    66\t   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/f3-test,\n    67\t   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/f3-test,\n    68\t   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/f3-test})\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- cst-catalog\n    72\t  \"The standard catalog plus the Python lowering behind a parse stage\n    73\t   that answers the precompiled packets.\"\n    74\t  []\n    75\t  (frontend/install (frontends/standard)\n    76\t                    cst-manifest\n    77\t                    {:parse (fn [source] (get packets source)),\n    78\t                     :lower python.repl/lower,\n    79\t                     :lower-session python.repl/lower-session,\n    80\t                     :display :output}))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn- session\n    84\t  \"A shell switched to `lang`, composed with `opts`.\"\n    85\t  ([lang] (session lang {}))\n    86\t  ([lang opts]\n    87\t   (first (repl/eval-input\n    88\t            (frontends/create-state (merge {:frontends (cst-catalog)} opts))\n    89\t            (str \"(lang \" lang \")\")))))\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\t(def ^:private langs\n    93\t  \"The ids every session scenario runs under: the precompiled packets on\n    94\t   every host, and the installed parser where it runs.\"\n    95\t  #?(:cljd [:yang.python/cst]\n    96\t     :clj [:yang.python/cst :yang.python/antlr]\n    97\t     :cljs [:yang.python/cst]))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- feed\n   101\t  \"Submit each line in order; every `[state text]` answered.\"\n   102\t  [state lines]\n   103\t  (rest (reductions (fn [[st _] line] (repl/eval-input st line))\n   104\t                    [state nil]\n   105\t                    lines)))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- texts\n   109\t  [state lines]\n   110\t  (mapv second (feed state lines)))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t;; =============================================================================\n   114\t;; Session scenarios (every host)\n   115\t;; =============================================================================\n   116\t\n   117\t(deftest ^:slow assignment-then-print-test\n   118\t  (slow/guard\n   119\t    \"assignment-then-print-test\"\n   120\t    (fn []\n   121\t      (doseq [lang langs]\n   122\t        (testing (str lang)\n   123\t          (let [[[assigned t1] [_ t2]] (feed (session lang) [\"x = 1\" \"print(x)\"])]\n   124\t            (is (= lang (:lang (session lang))))\n   125\t            (is (= [\"\" \"1\\n\"] [t1 t2]))\n     1\t(ns yin.repl.frontends\n     2\t  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n     3\t   8.5.6, slice F2): the three legacy hand-written frontends installed into\n     4\t   a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is the only place the REPL composition\n     5\t   names a language's namespace; `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the\n     6\t   catalog selects.\n     7\t\n     8\t   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n     9\t   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n    10\t   already read, else the source text.\"\n    11\t  (:require\n    12\t    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n    13\t    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n    14\t    [yang.php :as yang.php]\n    15\t    [yang.python :as yang.python]\n    16\t    [yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n    17\t    #?@(:cljd [] :clj [[yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n    18\t                       [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]])\n    19\t    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t(defn- manifest\n    23\t  [id language]\n    24\t  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n    25\t   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n    26\t   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n    27\t   :yang.frontend/language language,\n    28\t   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n    29\t                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n    30\t                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n    31\t   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n    32\t   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n    33\t   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n    34\t   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(defn- clojure-lower\n    38\t  [forms]\n    39\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n    40\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n    41\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t#?(:cljd nil\n    45\t   :clj\n    46\t   (defn- antlr-manifest\n    47\t     []\n    48\t     (assoc (manifest :yang.python/antlr :python.antlr)\n    49\t            :yang.frontend/revision \"f3\"\n    50\t            :yang.frontend/grammar\n    51\t            {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n    52\t             :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n    53\t             :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1})))\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn standard\n    57\t  \"The standard catalog. The Clojure frontend consumes the forms the\n    58\t   shell's own reader read, so its parse stage is the identity.  The Python\n    59\t   ANTLR frontend is installed where its parser runs (the JVM); elsewhere\n    60\t   selecting it answers `unavailable-parser`.  It shows what a submission\n    61\t   printed and not the program's value (`:display :output`).\"\n    62\t  []\n    63\t  (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n    64\t    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang.clojure/legacy :clojure)\n    65\t                           {:input :forms,\n    66\t                            :parse identity,\n    67\t                            :lower clojure-lower})\n    68\t    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang.python/legacy :python)\n    69\t                           {:parse identity, :lower yang.python/compile})\n    70\t    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang.php/legacy :php)\n    71\t                           {:parse identity, :lower yang.php/compile})\n    72\t    #?@(:cljd [] :clj [true (frontend/install\n    73\t                              (antlr-manifest)\n    74\t                              {:parse (fn [source]\n    75\t                                        (python.antlr.parser/parse-source\n    76\t                                          (str source \"\\n\"))),\n    77\t                               :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n    78\t                               :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n    79\t                               :display :output,\n    80\t                               :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})])))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn create-state\n    84\t  \"`yin.repl/create-state` composed with the standard catalog unless the\n    85\t   host supplies its own `:frontends`.\"\n    86\t  ([] (create-state {}))\n    87\t  ([opts]\n    88\t   (repl/create-state\n    89\t     (-> opts\n    90\t         (update :frontends #(or % (standard)))\n    91\t         (update :primitives #(merge python.antlr.repl/primitives %))))))\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792292000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-plan-review.prompt.md:38:   friction (the dynamic warnings class) blow the budget?\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792292000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-plan-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:13:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n 'JVM|helper|17\\\\\\\\.|L[1-4]|parser|grammar|target' docs/design/yang.typescript.md docs/design/yang.php.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"docs/design/yang.php.md:3:Status: Designed 2026-10-17. Implementation pending: no part of this frontend\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:47:to D7, the shared rulings (own null sentinel, Jing numeric kinds, JVM-only\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:50:PHP uses the lifted namespaces of `yang.typescript.md` section 17 (L1 to L4\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:62:`display_errors=stderr`. The grammar's feature set (enums, `match`,\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:109:  lowering targets `php/local-get`/`php/local-set` on the dict. All other\\ndocs/design/ya