{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/python/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc | head -85; rg -n 'warn|dynamic' src/cljd/dao/stream -g '*.cljd' | head -20; nl -ba docs/design/yang.typescript.md | sed -n '1515,1542p'; nl -ba docs/design/yang.php.md | sed -n '1290,1308p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc | sed -n '17,26p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test\n     2\t  \"The lowering on every host from hand-built CST packets: no parser needed,\n     3\t   so this runs on the JVM and on Node. Covers the unknown-rule refusal,\n     4\t   tree validation, a golden, and the stage transform's routing.\"\n     5\t  (:require\n     6\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     7\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n     8\t    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]))\n     9\t\n    10\t\n    11\t(defn packet\n    12\t  \"A CST packet from a nested form: `[rule child ...]` for a rule and\n    13\t   `[type text]` (type a string) for a token. Spans are zero-width: the\n    14\t   lowering reads them only for diagnostics. Ids are preorder, as the\n    15\t   parser numbers them, so generated names match a parsed packet's.\"\n    16\t  [form]\n    17\t  (let [out (volatile! [])]\n    18\t    (letfn [(walk\n    19\t              [f]\n    20\t              (let [id (count @out)]\n    21\t                (if (string? (first f))\n    22\t                  (vswap! out conj {:id id, :kind :token, :type (first f),\n    23\t                                    :text (second f), :span [0 0]})\n    24\t                  (do (vswap! out conj nil)\n    25\t                      (let [kids (mapv walk (rest f))]\n    26\t                        (vswap! out assoc id {:id id, :kind :rule,\n    27\t                                              :rule (name (first f)),\n    28\t                                              :children kids, :span [0 0]}))))\n    29\t                id))]\n    30\t      (walk form))\n    31\t    {:yang.cst/version 1,\n    32\t     :yang.cst/unit [:hand 0],\n    33\t     :yang.cst/grammar \"hand\",\n    34\t     :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok,\n    35\t     :yang.cst/root 0,\n    36\t     :yang.cst/nodes @out,\n    37\t     :yang.cst/complete true}))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- chain\n    41\t  \"Single-child rule chain from `rules` down to `leaf`.\"\n    42\t  [rules leaf]\n    43\t  (reduce (fn [inner r] [r inner]) leaf (reverse rules)))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(def ^:private expr-chain\n    47\t  [:testlist_star_expr :test :or_test :and_test :not_test :comparison :expr\n    48\t   :atom_expr :atom])\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn- statement\n    52\t  [expr-stmt]\n    53\t  [:stmt [:simple_stmts [:simple_stmt expr-stmt] [\"NEWLINE\" \"\\n\"]]])\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(def ^:private x-equals-1\n    57\t  (packet [:file_input\n    58\t           (statement [:expr_stmt\n    59\t                       (chain expr-chain [:name [\"NAME\" \"x\"]])\n    60\t                       [\"ASSIGN\" \"=\"]\n    61\t                       (chain expr-chain [\"NUMBER\" \"1\"])])\n    62\t           [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]]))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(deftest hand-packet-golden-test\n    66\t  (is (= (u/then (u/app (u/v 'py/global-set) (u/v '%globals)\n    67\t                        (u/lit {:py/str \"x\"}) (u/lit 1))\n    68\t                 (u/lit :py/None))\n    69\t         (lower/lower-module-body x-equals-1))))\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(defn- refusal\n    73\t  [pk]\n    74\t  (try (lower/lower-module-body pk)\n    75\t       nil\n    76\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo :cljs ExceptionInfo) e\n    77\t         (select-keys (ex-data e) [:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :rule]))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(deftest unknown-rule-fails-qualified-test\n    81\t  (testing \"a rule with no arm is never dropped: the error names it\"\n    82\t    (is (= {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/unhandled-rule,\n    83\t            :rule \"no_such_rule\"}\n    84\t           (refusal (packet [:file_input [:stmt [:no_such_rule]]\n    85\t                             [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]])))))\n  1515\t## 17. The yang.core lift enumeration\n  1516\t\n  1517\tWhat TypeScript pulls from `yang.python` into shared namespaces (lifts L1 to\n  1518\tL4; PHP uses the same namespaces):\n  1519\t\n  1520\t- `yang.core.prelude`: the emitter machinery (define, strip, placeholder, wide\n  1521\t  application, exports, module-spec resolution) and `admit` (L1).\n  1522\t- `yang.core.uast`: from `yang.python.antlr.uast`, renamed (L2).\n  1523\t- `yang.core.lower`: `gen`, `kids`, `rules`, `rule-kids`, `site`, `app*`,\n  1524\t  `contains-rule?`, and the diagnostic builders `unsupported!`, `syntax!`,\n  1525\t  `default-arm` with the namespace and refusal table as parameters (L2).\n  1526\t- `yang.core.stage`: `diagnostic`, `lower-transform`, `open-stage`,\n  1527\t  `step-stage`, parameterized by the ok-check, the lower function and the\n  1528\t  diagnostic namespace (L2).\n  1529\t- `yang.core.names`: `canonicalize` (L2, section 6.3).\n  1530\t- `yang.antlr.packet`: D1 fixed (L2).\n  1531\t- `yang.core.module`: `module-symbol` (prefix parameter), `require-node`,\n  1532\t  `module-tree`, `declare-free-name`, and the `module-spec` and\n  1533\t  `scc-module-specs` shapes (L3).\n  1534\t- `yang.core.publication`: `publication-order`, `publish-units!`, with\n  1535\t  `imported-names`, `module-spec` and `scc-module-specs` injected, plus the\n  1536\t  binder-table emission hook (L3).\n  1537\t- `yang.core.claims`: `append-claims!` and the evidence record (L3, exercised\n  1538\t  in T10).\n  1539\t- `yin.repl.frontends`: binding `:primitives` (L4).\n  1540\t\n  1541\t**Not lifted now**: the prelude *definitions* (the escape machinery `ctx`,\n  1542\t`frame`, `raise`, `unwind-to`, `try`, `try-finally`, `call-ec`; the generator\n  1290\t\n  1291\t- `:yang.php/antlr` is installed beside `:yang.php/legacy` in\n  1292\t  `yin.repl.frontends/standard`, with no fallback.\n  1293\t- Every program in `test/yang/php_test.clj` is re-expressed in the new corpus,\n  1294\t  with expectations corrected where the legacy was wrong (`null` is\n  1295\t  `:php/null`, not `nil`).\n  1296\t- The browser demo `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/compilation_pipeline.cljs`\n  1297\t  compiles editable PHP synchronously in CLJS with the legacy frontend, while\n  1298\t  the ANTLR parser is JVM-only. The demo moves to **checked-in CST packets**\n  1299\t  for its sample programs (generated by a JVM script, the `dht-import-v1.edn`\n  1300\t  pattern), lowered and run parserless in the browser; editable PHP source in\n  1301\t  the demo is dropped, or routed to a configured parser service when one\n  1302\t  exists (owner decision B8.9). `src/dev/subsystems.edn` is a one-line\n  1303\t  retarget.\n  1304\t- `:yang.php/legacy` retires at P8 (file deleted, no shim; the repository has\n  1305\t  no backward-compatibility obligation) once the demo retarget has landed and\n  1306\t  the corpus covers the legacy programs (owner decision B8.6).\n  1307\t\n  1308\tWhat stays refused after migration: `goto`; return by reference (corner C7);\n    17\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    18\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n    19\t            [yin.repl.adapter :as adapter]\n    20\t            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n    21\t            [yin.repl :as repl]\n    22\t            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n    23\t            [yin.repl.host :as host]))\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\t(def line-key :yin.repl.input/line)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
